### @-mention syntax (TAPD-specific)

Use `[~user_name]` (the literal characters) where `user_name` is the **TAPD
username** — e.g. `[~zhangsan]`. NOT `@zhangsan`, NOT `@id:1000`.

Look up the username via `cache.json:knownUsers` first; if not present, call
`tapd_users_list` once and let the comment skill cache the result back.

## Project-specific values: always probe

These fields have **project-specific enums** that you cannot hardcode:

- `status` (every entity) — call `tapd_workflows_list` first
- `module` (bugs) — call `tapd_modules_list`
- `category_id` (stories) — call `tapd_categories_list`
- Custom fields — call `tapd_custom-fields_list`

Never guess an enum literal. If the user asks for "把状态改成已解决", look up
the actual `resolved` (or `已解决`) string the workspace uses, and confirm in
the preview block before writing.

## Pagination & batching

- All `_list` tools accept `limit` (default 30, max 200) and `page` (1-indexed).
- For full-set fetches, paginate until the page returns < `limit` rows.
- Bulk write operations are capped at 10 per confirmation —
  see `tapd-safety-rules` HARD-RULE-5.

## Time format

- `spentdate`, `due`, `begin` → `YYYY-MM-DD` (string)
- `created`, `modified` → `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`
- Timezone is the workspace's local tz (typically Asia/Shanghai for TAPD)
